content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent cycle interval: footnote 1 says cycle 6 should occur at least 59 days from day 1 of cycle 5, but cycles 6-9 are 12-week cycles (84 days), and footnote 12 says day 85 is end-of-cycle tumor assessment, implying 84-day cycles.",
      "page": 61,
      "quote": "Should occur at least 59 days from the previous day 1 of cycle 5 (for cycle 6), or 81 days from day 1 of previous cycle (for cycles 7 – 9), and no sooner than 18 days after the previous dose.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contradictory EOS biopsy timing: footnote 1 says post-treatment biopsy can be obtained within 28 days of last dose, but footnote 5 in Table 6 says EOS tumor biopsy at progression within 28 days of imaging that documented progression; these may conflict if progression occurs later than 28 days after last dose.",
      "page": 61,
      "quote": "The only posttreatment assessment that can occur outside of this timeframe is the post treatment biopsy (required in Group 2) that can be obtained at any time within 28 days of last dose of cemiplimab.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent retreatment duration: Section 8.1.5 says retreatment is four 12-week cycles (48 weeks) but also says 'cemiplimab IV 350 mg Q3W' which is every 3 weeks, not 12-week cycles; also Table 5 is for cycles 6-9, not retreatment cycles.",
      "page": 67,
      "quote": "resumption of treatment with cemiplimab IV 350 mg Q3W will be allowed per Table 5 (four 12-week cycles).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing footnote 13 in Table 6: Table 6 has a superscript '13' on 'Extended Follow-up' but footnotes only go to 12.",
      "page": 63,
      "quote": "Every 4 months for 1 year13",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent follow-up visit numbering: Table 6 lists 'Follow-up 71' but footnote 1 says after completion of this schedule, patients followed quarterly; footnote 9 mentions follow-up visits 1, 4, and 7, but the table has 7 follow-up visits plus extended follow-up, so 'Follow-up 71' is likely a typo.",
      "page": 63,
      "quote": "Follow-up 71",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent imaging schedule in Table 6: CT/MRI row shows X at Follow-up 1, 4, 5, 6, 7 but not at 2, 3; footnote 10 says scans linked to follow-up visits required only if PD not confirmed, but no explanation for missing visits 2 and 3.",
      "page": 63,
      "quote": "CT/MRI (chest/abdomen/pelvis) And/or digital photography10 X X X X",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent PK/ADA collection: Table 6 shows PK at Follow-up 1, 4, 7 and ADA at 1 and 7, but footnote 9 says 'PK is not required at the EOS visit if it was collected at follow-up visit 1 and follow-up visit 4' – but EOS visit is not in Table 6; also footnote 9 says ADA not required at EOS if collected at FU1, but EOS is not listed in Table 6.",
      "page": 65,
      "quote": "Cemiplimab PK samples will be collected at follow-up visits 1, 4, and 7. ADA samples will be collected at follow-up visits 1 and 7. ADA is not required at the EOS visit if it was collected at follow-up visit 1. PK is not required at the EOS visit if it was collected at follow-up visit 1 and follow-up visit 4.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent AE collection period: Footnote 12 says nonserious AE and SAE data collected until 30 days after last dose, but footnote 11 says any cancer treatments recorded until 105 days after last dose; also Section 8.1.4 says patients with PD followed for survival until death, but AE collection stops at 30 days.",
      "page": 66,
      "quote": "Nonserious AE and SAE data will be collected from the day of informed consent until 30 days after the last dose of cemiplimab.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent retreatment eligibility: Section 8.1.5 says patients who complete 9 cycles without progression and then progress during follow-up visits 1-7 may resume treatment, but Section 8.1.4 says patients who discontinue due to reasons other than PD continue follow-up until PD or completion of follow-up visits 1-7; this is consistent but retreatment says 'without any intervening systemic anticancer therapy' but does not specify if prior PD is allowed.",
      "page": 67,
      "quote": "For patients (Group 1 or Group 2) who complete 9 cycles of treatment without disease progression and subsequently experience disease progression during the follow-up period (follow-up visits 1 through 7 only) without any intervening systemic anticancer therapy, resumption of treatment with cemiplimab IV 350 mg Q3W will be allowed",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent screening brain MRI: Section 8.2.1 says brain MRI required at screening if not performed in prior 60 days, but Section 8.1.5 says retreatment patients must repeat all screening activities with exception of brain MRI, implying brain MRI not required for retreatment; this is a contradiction.",
      "page": 68,
      "quote": "Brain MRI, with gadolinium, is required at screening if it has not performed in the prior 60 days.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent imaging modality for Group 2: Section 8.2.1 says baseline radiologic assessment includes CT chest preferably with contrast, but Section 8.2.2 says for Group 2, radiologic imaging of anatomic area of externally visible target lesions should be performed at screening and each response assessment, but does not mention CT chest; also Section 8.2.1 says if CT chest identifies metastatic lesion, patient assigned to Group 1, but Section 8.2.2 says Group 2 patients may have radiologic imaging of target lesions, which could include chest.",
      "page": 69,
      "quote": "Baseline radiologic assessment will also include CT chest, preferably with contrast (If CT chest identifies a metastatic lesion, the patient should be assigned to Group 1).",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent response criteria: Section 8.2.2 says irRC can inform decision to continue treatment, but also says irRC data not included in primary endpoint; however, it does not specify how irRC is used for response assessment in Group 2, which uses composite criteria (Appendix 2) not irRC.",
      "page": 70,
      "quote": "To account for the possibility of unconventional immune responses, immune-related response criteria (irRC) (Nishino 2013) can inform the decision regarding whether to continue treatment for an individual patient if the investigator believes it is in the best clinical interest of the patient, after discussion and approval from the medical monitor.",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
